@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Active sale lines and safe removal
+
+## Ownership and pinned integration baseline
+
+Phase 2 owns the durable line-removal representation. This patch is prepared locally,
+with no remote branch update, against integration commit
+`078070e156a53004efe007f6011bd01da68298e7`:
+
+- Payment #1363: `990cb7a7ccaf837dc3672d09a85b7f1a74526696`.
+- Safety #1377: `d7c2306db3d58e6d470ff93679efec838ad8bb71`, including shell #1375
+  at `9c25673026b939304f5e599a62bf3b0d6ced5ede`.
+
+The local baseline merges the two feature branches. Conflict resolution keeps the
+payment branch's tender input and historical manual-card compatibility, its
+uncertainty/recovery condition and day-close actor projection. It also retains the
+safety branch's prescription release gates and prescription-action button.
+No branch is merged to develop. These local commits are a review/integration
+artifact; they are not permission to publish or to change another active branch.
+
+## Durable representation
+
+`PharmacySaleLine` gains nullable `removedAt`, `removedByUserId` and
+`removalReason`. An active line is exactly `removedAt IS NULL`.
+
+Use `ACTIVE_SALE_LINE` from `src/lib/pharmacy/active-sale-line.ts` in Prisma
+predicates. Raw SQL uses `"removedAt" IS NULL`. In-memory legacy projections use
+`isActiveSaleLine`. Existing database rows default to null and stay active.
+A removal marker is immutable and cannot be cleared. Original quantities, money,
+prescription references and append-only allocations remain unchanged.
+
+Migration `20261106100000_pharmacy_sale_line_removal` depends on the payment
+migrations through `20261106070000_pharmacy_payment_attempt_handoff`. It updates
+the preparation balance trigger, protects clinical inserts against removed lines,
+and writes a database-generated `LINE_REMOVED` sale event. It requires an exact
+linked stock reversal before the tombstone, and controlled restorations must also
+have their matching register correction. No repricing or discount rule is added.
+
+## Mutation contract
+
+`pharmacySales.removeLine` accepts `branchId`, `saleId`, `saleLineId`, a nonempty
+reason (up to 500 characters), and optional `controlledWitness` containing the
+existing staff-profile ID and PIN. It uses current counter/member/branch admission.
+PIN input is omitted from request audit evidence.
+
+The domain operation owns no transaction: the authorized router supplies one and
+retains its scoped sale lock through COMMIT. Its first database operation calls
+`pharmacy_assert_no_payment_attempt(organizationId, branchId, saleId)`.
+Released/settled attempts do not establish that a bill is unpaid: the operation
+separately requires OPEN status, no issued receipt/completion, no tender or refund,
+and no customer-order attachment. A line with return evidence or inconsistent
+allocation/movement evidence also fails closed.
+
+A duplicate retry on the same unpaid open sale returns `replayed: true`, without
+another reversal or audit event. The tombstone itself supplies the durable retry
+identity. A retry after payment is conservatively refused by the paid-sale checks.
+All original stock movements are reversed exactly once in the same lot, location,
+disposition and pack arrangement, using the existing stock-ledger primitive.
+
+Controlled lines require current dispensing authority and the existing fresh,
+independent pharmacist witness PIN. Missing original controlled-register source
+evidence refuses removal. Each restoration appends a witnessed correction linked
+to the original sale entry and the compensating stock movement. Historical
+prescription fills and review decisions are retained; removal does not free a
+prescription repeat or erase an emergency-supply history. A wrong PIN commits its
+existing lockout accounting through the router's blocked-result path, before any
+stock mutation.
+
+## Readers and phase 4 integration
+
+The patch filters preparation (SQL and application), checkout totals, completion,
+receipts, sale postings, stock/batch safety, loyalty, day close, returns, purchase
+history and analytical consumers. Void reversals exclude removed lines, avoiding
+a second reversal. Existing evidence/audit rows remain available as history.
+Preparation and provider dispatch also retain the safety branch's verified-prescription release gate before exposing instructions or collecting. Clinical queues hide removed lines; new review decisions, substitutions and
+sale-linked prescription fills serialize on the sale lock and reject removed
+lines. Prescription attachment cannot reactivate a tombstone.
+
+For the forthcoming #1377 scan binding:
+
+1. Keep scan and binding evidence immutable and reference the retained sale-line
+   ID. Removal must not delete scans, binding rows, allocations or clinical history.
+2. Under the same scoped sale lock, query the bound line using organization,
+   branch, sale and line identity plus `ACTIVE_SALE_LINE`. Re-read after locking.
+3. Payment and confirmed-mismatch checks must consider bindings only on active
+   lines. A removed mismatch remains historical evidence and does not remain a
+   payable line or block a different active pack.
+4. Bind/verify versus removal must serialize on that sale lock. An operation that
+   obtains the lock after removal must refuse the inactive line; no client flag or
+   manual-sale shortcut may reactivate it. Manual sales and missing-evidence
+   unverified states retain the already agreed policy.
+
+## Integration and rollout
+
+Integrate the pinned payment and safety foundations first in a local review
+checkout, retaining their respective behavior as described above. Apply the entire
+removal patch there, including the migration and all readers, and regenerate
+Prisma. Do not cherry-pick only the mutation or only the marker. Rebase/retest if
+any pinned head changes. The same SQL/body change belongs in #1363/#1372's shared
+payment core when those existing branches are reconciled; do not invent a second
+preparation balance calculation.
+
+The schema change is additive, but an old server does not know to exclude
+removed lines. Do not enable/call removal until every serving reader is on the
+coordinated implementation. No remove button, quantity editing, unit conversion,
+repricing, held-bill recovery or pack-binding implementation is included in this
+prerequisite backend patch. Keep existing PRs draft pending owner integration,
+UI wiring, race tests for the new scan binding and normal release review.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Node 22 typecheck and changed-file ESLint pass.
+- Complete migrations apply to a new isolated PostgreSQL 16 database.
+- Restricted runtime asserts `NOSUPERUSER` and `NOBYPASSRLS`.
+- 36 removal and existing payment-attempt database tests pass. The suites cover preparation/removal
+  in both lock orders, duplicate concurrent retries, transaction rollback,
+  partially paid/held/completed refusal, tenant and branch denial, actual router
+  membership/branch admission, controlled authority/PIN/lockout/register correction,
+  retained allocation evidence, clinical inserts, receipt exclusion and live report
+  SQL. No production data, provider, money or device is used.
+- Focused reader regressions: 249 pass and one existing report-catalog assertion
+  fails (expects 23 metrics; the foundation has 24). The identical 17-pass/1-fail
+  report test result reproduces at the unchanged pinned integration baseline.
+- An additional 178 focused sales/settlement/clinical tests pass.
+- No browser/Studio QA is claimed for this backend-only prerequisite.
